<title>SWITZERLAND: Ascom says Q1 orders up, sees good 1997.</title>
<headline>Ascom says Q1 orders up, sees good 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss telecommunications group Ascom Holding AG said orders in the first quarter were clearly higher than a year ago but sales were slightly lower in the period.</p>
<p>Ascom forecast a satisfactory full year in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Incoming orders in the first quarter of 1997 were clearly higher than the corresponding year-ago quarter, while sales were slightly lower,&quot; an Ascom statement said.  </p>
<p>&quot;Ascom expects business to go satisfactorily in 1997,&quot; it added without elaborating.</p>
<p>Ascom reported in the same stament 1996 net group loss of 128 million Swiss francs.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
